{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310814,"nonce":"pnK+03BBJlOJ4L+tEBV/7/N4PpY=","title":"cranelift amode-CSE PR","message":"Upstream cranelift PR #13766 (aarch64 amode: share `base+index` across loads by folding a non-zero uimm12 offset into the load immediate + keeping base+index CSE-able) is a **NO-OP for rayzor's current wasm**, confirmed by DISASM of /tmp/q4.cwasm (RAYZOR_WASM_CWASM_DUMP), not by measurement.\n\nWhy: every vector load in the Q4 dot kernel (subDotVec→q4DotMA4) disassembles to `ldr q, [base, w_index, uxtw]` — RegExtended, **offset 0**. rayzor computes the full displacement INTO the i32 index in-guest (`wBase + Usize.fromInt(wOff + half*16)` then `.load(ptr)` → wasm `v128.load offset=0`), so cranelift never sees a non-zero static offset. My PR's rule 10 deliberately preserves the offset-0 single-instruction form, so it correctly does nothing here.\n\n**The real rayzor-side lever (THE wasm load lever):** make wasm_backend emit `v128.load offset=N (base+idx)` (static wasm load offsets) instead of folding N into the in-guest i32 address. subDotVec's two loads are `wBase+wOff+0` and `wBase+wOff+16` — they SHARE `wBase+wOff` and differ by 16, but rayzor emits two independent indices. With static offsets, cranelift (and the now-merged amode CSE) collapse them to one `add base,idx,uxtw` + two immediate-offset loads. Secondary: cranelift even recomputes `add x8, x0, #0x10` per load (base+const CSE miss) — same root, disappears once base+idx is shared.\n\nMEASUREMENT-MODE GOTCHA (burned me 2026-06-30, cost an hour): `rayzor run \u003cf\u003e` defaults to DEBUG + Cranelift JIT. For the q4bench that gave native 30× — a frame-tracking (`fn22`/rayzor_update_call_frame_location, enable_stack_traces=true) artifact in the hot loop, NOT a real gap. Native PARITY needs BOTH flags: `--llvm --release` → haxe_ma4 0.263ms = **1.12× rust** (dot-work 0.199ms, faster than rust). Tiers on q4bench: `run` (debug cranelift) 30×; `--release` (cranelift, no frame-track) 3.9×; `--llvm --release` (LLVM-tier SDOT) 1.12×. WASM is mode-independent (no frame-tracking; `--wasm` == `--wasm --release` == 3.44×). ALWAYS pass `--llvm --release` for native perf claims. So: NATIVE is DONE (parity); WASM 3.44× is the only real residual, and per [[perf_haxe_qmatmul_blocked_on_simd_inlining]] it's the cranelift-vs-LLVM floor (~23 instr/sdot vs Rust ~8: nibble-unpack + address-math cranelift won't strength-reduce) — largely UPSTREAM, not a rayzor-side fix. Bonus bug found: unrolling subDotVec (straight-line SIMD) fails wasm validation (\"block with value...types\") — minimal 2-load case compiles, so the trigger is narrow; blocks the unroll the static-offset peel would need.\n\nPROCESS GOTCHA (the invalid measurement): editing a cargo GIT-checkout (`~/.cargo/git/checkouts/.../inst.isle`) does NOT recompile — cargo fingerprints git deps by REV, not file content; `cargo clean -p cranelift-codegen` + rebuild reused the cached .rlib (mtime pre-dated the build, no \"Compiling cranelift-codegen\" line). To test a local cranelift change against rayzor, use a `[patch.crates-io]` PATH dep (content-fingerprinted), not a checkout edit. Related: [[perf_wasm_v8_vs_wasmtime_2x]] (the cranelift-vs-LLVM floor on the non-dot ~30%).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_wasm_amode_pr_noop_static_offset_lever` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}